[test-assertion] [test-assertion] The new --required-cycles CLI flag is untested: no test invokes the CLI to exercise the argparse wiring (explicit value overriding gate.yaml) or the req < 1 stderr + EXIT_CLI_ERROR branch. The added tests only call run_verify directly, so a CLI-only regression would go unnoticed.
[test-assertion] [test-assertion] test_it_is_the_LAST_n_cycles_that_are_checked writes clean cycles 1 and 7 with required_cycles=1. This catches an implementation that hard-codes last_three, but it would also pass if the implementation checked the first N cycles, because cycle 1 is clean. The test's docstring says 'older broken cycle' but no older cycle is actually broken; making cycle 1 invalid would make the LAST-n behavior stronger.
[test-assertion] [test-assertion] read_required_cycles has untested fallback branches for a non-dict YAML root and a non-dict verify section. Tests cover missing gate, missing verify section, malformed YAML, and bad scalar values, but not data=[...] or verify=[...], leaving those two defensive branches unexercised.
